1
00:07:43,333 --> 00:07:49,333
In the beginning there was Bombolini the fool, Bombolini the drunk, Bombolini the joke. In the end there was Bombolini
the mayor, Bombolini the hero, Bombolini the beautiful. In between is the secret of Santa Vittoria.

2
00:15:26,666 --> 00:15:32,666
The Secret of Santa Vittoria is a comedy, drama,
war film directed by Stanley Kramer.

3
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:16,000
During World War II, Italian villagers hide their wine from the German army.

4
00:30:53,333 --> 00:30:59,333
Italo Bombolini, played by Anthony Quinn.

5
00:38:36,666 --> 00:38:42,666
Rosa, played by Anna Magnani.

6
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:26,000
Fabio, played by Giancarlo Giannini.

7
00:54:03,333 --> 00:54:09,333
Caterina Malatesta, played by Virna Lisi.

8
01:01:46,666 --> 01:01:52,666
Capt. von Prum, played by Hardy Krüger.

9
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:36,000
Feldwebel Zopf, played by Wolfgang Jansen.

10
01:17:13,333 --> 01:17:19,333
The Secret of Santa Vittoria is a 1969 American war
film distributed by United Artists.

11
01:24:56,666 --> 01:25:02,666
It was produced and directed by Stanley Kramer and co-produced by George
Glass from a screenplay by Ben Maddow and William Rose.

12
01:32:40,000 --> 01:32:46,000
It was based on the best-selling 1966 novel by Robert Crichton.

13
01:40:23,333 --> 01:40:29,333
The music score was by Ernest Gold and the cinematography by Giuseppe Rotunno.

14
01:48:06,666 --> 01:48:12,666
The film stars Anthony Quinn, Anna Magnani, Virna
Lisi, Hardy Krüger, and Sergio Franchi.

15
01:55:50,000 --> 01:55:56,000
It also features Renato Rascel, Giancarlo Giannini, and Eduardo Ciannelli;
with Valentina Cortese making an uncredited appearance.

16
02:03:33,333 --> 02:03:39,333
It was shot almost entirely on location in Anticoli Corrado, Italy (near Rome).

17
02:11:16,666 --> 02:11:22,666
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
